  "body": "Follow-up filed from the Phase 3 closing audit of design #4592 (issue #4593, task 14247), at origin/main .\n\n## Gap\n\n () never checks that each payload entry's required journal version is at or below the frame's .  (replication.rs:379) proves only that every line decodes as a .\n\n demands the opposite:  () refuses any entry whose  () exceeds the journal header version — e.g. an  entry (requires version 2, or 4 with a persisted budget) under a version-1 header.\n\nSo a signed, in-range snapshot can carry an entry kind its header version does not admit. The verified cursor advances over it, the durable receiver commits it, and the replica then refuses its own journal at the next restore — the same brick-at-next-open shape Phase 1 of #4592 closed for version-0 envelopes (see the comment at replication.rs:740-744). Restore refuses the journal whole, so no impossible world state is ever applied; the defect is admission, not application.\n\nA real writer can never produce this frame (the writer bumps the header before appending such an entry,  contract on ), so this is a writer-bug / forged-stream hole of exactly the class #4471, #4486 and #4487 closed leg by leg.\n\n## Fix shape (for the implementing task, not this audit)\n\nIn , before chaining a Snapshot/Tail payload, refuse any entry whose  exceeds , with a typed  (a dedicated variant or -adjacent — implementer's call, recorded on the PR). Add regression tests mirroring : an in-range snapshot and tail carrying an over-version entry are refused with tracker state untouched.\n\n## Sibling observation from the same inventory\n\nCheckpoint-parts ordering (parts immediately followed by their , enforced in ) is likewise restore-only. It is NOT part of this fix: parts and their checkpoint can span frame boundaries, so a per-frame  check cannot decide it. Triage may split it into a receiver/commit-path check if wanted.\n\n## Links\n\n- Audit: issue #4593 (full inventory + dispositions (a)–(d))\n- Design: issue #4592; contract statement landed in the  module doc by the #4593 PR\n",
